Back in June I managed to ascend a 10-conduct monk in Eidolos' NAO
tournament and over the next few months started thinking about whether
an 11-conduct hero was feasible.  I've never tried pacifist so that
only left foodless.  I had quite a few false starts and was basically
going on the wrong track in worrying about what starting spells my
wizards had.  Then in Dev Null I lost several 10-conduct monks to
stupid maneuvers (falling in pits with cockatrice corpses, etc.) and
then nopsled took the trophy.  So, I figured I would try something
novel since I hadn't seen an eleven conduct ascension in either the
Dev Null or June NAO tournaments.  I failed but I was determined to
ascend.  It had dawned on me that a wizard's combat prowess was
actually not all that bad, despite only being able to advance to basic
in unarmed combat ... it's all about the daggers.  The lack of
intrinsics was a challenge but certainly not insurmountable.  To
prevent starvation I used same-race polyself throughout the game.  And
so began the startscumming ...

Rerolling:
http://alt.org/nethack/player-all.php?player=Tenaya11
I started a new nickname on NAO so that I could track my progress and,
as you can see, of the 226 games started, I only tried to play 12
(maybe 13 but can't remember about game 1).  I played wizards since my
criteria for playing a character was that I start with a ring of slow
digestion and at least one of the following: ring of polymorph
control, or potion, wand or ring of polymorph.  The ideal case was to
have a starting ring of polymorph control since finding a means of
polymorph is statistically easier than finding the ring of polymorph
control.  Also the wizard's starting cloak made hunting for poly-traps
much safer.  Spells and wands were just gravy if they were good and
the only useful scroll of course was scare monster.

The Plan (in a nutshell):
I figured that with a pet, careful play, and a stack of daggers I
could stay alive maintaining my conducts and not use too much
nutrition.  While leveling up to increase my Hp, acquiring some good
armor and daggers, I needed to find a ring of polymorph before my
17,000 turns of nutrition was used up.  After that I just had to set
up a pudding farm and get stacks of loot.  I figured that I would end
up with all the armor that I wanted but without much enchantment, and
of course no dragon scale mail.  I did find a GDSM in a bones pile but
didn't want to use it.  With a lot of HP and wands from the farm I
planned on zapping my way across the Astral Plane.  And that's
basically what happened.  Obviously this plan wouldn't have worked for
a pacifist since there is no pudding farming for the pacifist.

The Beginning:
I played an orc for the poison resistance and due to the low int and
consequent hunger consumption I avoided casting spells.  At times I
was too conservative and should have used force bolt instead of dying
to ants and bats and foxes.  With a starting ring of slow digestion, I
only had 17,000 turns to find a means of same-race polymorphing.  So,
I made my way to Sokoban and used my pet to B/U/C identify my rings
and if cursed, I would fountain dip.  In my final game I was fortunate
indeed to start out with a wand of enlightenment but would have price-
id'ed if I hadn't had the wand.  Staying alive was not too hard if I
played carefully, which I did in 1 of 12 (or 13) games.  In one game I
opened a box and got my ring of SD zapped.  In the other YASD's I
should have played more carefully or used my pet better, or whatever.
But the deaths certainly seemed my fault rather than the RNG being too
difficult.
I usually wound up with a motley collection of daggers and threw them
as often as possible and eventually got my skill up high enough to
feel safe in the mines.  Once I had collected some gnomish daggers I
was finally able to build up a decent sized stack of daggers; until
then I had like 6 separate stacks of daggers in my inventory (orcish,
elven, and regular and of all different + and B/U/C).
One windfall was finding a +2 dwarvish mithril coat that I wore for
the entire game.  I was considering switching to dragon scale mail for
intrinsics but seeing how much punishment I would get in melee I opted
instead for the better AC.  Intrinsics were handled by a full set of
rings and switching them at opportune times.

In a ranger bones pile I found a rotted +2 cloak of displacement but I
didn't wear it until I got to Astral.  Until then I kept on my
starting cloak of magic resistance because I needed a guaranteed
source of MR.  Once I woke up the Wizard I kept my Eye of the
Aethiopica in a bag.

(Thanks jspeed although despite reading your YASD, I've still had my
Quest Atifact stolen).

Pudding Agriculture:
In my November 11-conduct attempt I realized that I had probably been
unprepared for the ascension run and even though I quit due to
inadvertently cancelling my Bell of Opening, I probably would not have
survived the Astral Plane.  So, once I found a ring of polymorph to go
with my ring of polymorph control I set up a pudding farm on level
15.  This was my first attempt at farming and I was amazed at how easy
it was.  Being able to hold down ^A to repeatedly swing my thoroughly
corroded lockpick for 1000 turns at a time did not seem very
sporting.  But, there is a reason for death drops and if the dungeon
doesn't give a single potion of holy water, it's nice to know there is
a way to acquire it.  I had a specific wish-list from my pudding farm
and 100,000 turns of it gave me all of the potions, rings, wands and
scrolls of scare monster that I could need.  I also acquired 3 crystal
balls (much needed), boots of lev, boots of speed, +1 helm of
telepathy, +1 gloves of power.  Noticeably missing items that were
missed much on Astral were boots of jumping and a helm of opposite
alignment.

Finishing touches:
I had planned on using a high-level purple worm after the farm to
handle liches and loot the Valley of the Dead for me but of course
Purple Burple ate a chameleon soon after I got him.  I was spared the
effort of polytrap dancing by finding a magic harp.  I soon realized
that with an unlimited supply of holy water (100+), scrolls of scare
monster, and plenty of daggers, liches weren't a problem.  I even
meleed minotaurs with an AC=--4 and despite losing a couple hundred HP
to each one I was just fine because I had alchemised my way up over
500HP.

So, I found all of the stairs in Gehennom with some help from the
resident liches and lucked out in that an ice box was on level 3.  I
used my wands of create monster until I had a cockatrice corpse for my
trip to the Plane of Earth.  Also next to the ice box I left 60
blessed potions of fruit juice.  I left some at the vibrating square
too.  Oh yeah, and I had pudding farmed/alchemised 41 cursed potions
of gain level ... getting to the planes was easy.

I reasoned that even with Herculean HP and several amulets of life
saving I could still die or be heavily inconvenienced if I spent too
too much time during the ascension run.  I was also quite nervous when
I had my polyself ring set on as suddenly a mis-key could turn me into
something other than an orc.  With 100,000 turns already gone I was
playing quite fast and thus when the time came to polyself I put both
rings on and then, in a safe place, typed "n500."  the controlled
polymorph always stops the waiting.  But I did not want to do such a
stunt with Rodney after me so I switched to a juice diet once I had
killed Rodney (courtesy of the countless potions of sickness, see
invisible, fruit juice, and just plain old water from my farming days)
and did my last self-poly right before grabbing a cockatrice corpse
from his zoo.

The Astral Plane was difficult because I couldn't get Pestilence out
of the doorway and a lich and a titan kept summoning monsters.
Usually I have jumping boots but without them I couldn't get around
Pestilence's corpse and had to revive him with a teleport zap.  I had
plenty of amulets of lifesaving and scrolls of scare monster so I was
never too concerned.  With a ring of conflict and judicious teleport
zaps I managed to clear a lane through the plane and made my way to
all three altars.

That's probably more than enough description.  Sorry this was so long.

